## 6. TimeCap risk

  TimeCap is a capability token. It grants wall-clock access.
  `now_ms` reads that token and returns integer milliseconds.

  Plan stop rule: if TimeCap on CLI main fails seed typecheck,
  COORD stops ship 3. Do not fall back to `date`.

  RT proof (`audit/plan3_rt.oot`): TimeCap on main: YES.

  Seed check of scratch
  `/tmp/grok-goal-e3250e659225/implementer/timecap_main_cli_shape.oo`
  prints `OK` and exits 0. Shape:

    pub fn main(fs: &FsCap, sys: &SysCap, time: &TimeCap, args: List[String])

  Seed emit-c injects `time = oo_cap_grant_time();` and
  lowers `now_ms(time)` to `oo_now_ms(time)`.

  COORD does not stop ship 3 for TimeCap.

  Residual risk: the official seed rebuild of the full CLI
  still fails on `oo_fs_rmdir`. Wave 1 may edit locked files.
  INT cannot prove a seed-built `bin/ooda` until the check
  host accepts the 51-module graph. Parent decides the host.
  Do not patch oodac. Do not patch chs_rt.

  LLVM emit of TimeCap is residual. Product path is C emit
  plus gcc.

